From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: keep a command entry's submit copy at a refresh when it walks clean (EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY, test aid EDEN_TEST_FRAME_WAIT_MS), off by default

What: on a first start (run1233, 12 Nov) the present gave up its 4 s frame wait three times while
the graphics side was ~25 s behind; the game ran ~25 fence steps ahead and the hand-over refresh
(DmaPusher::Push, dma_pusher.h) read every entry of a waited list from memory again, unjudged:
221 entries held later frames' words, junk followed and a junk shape type crashed. With
EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY=2 both refreshes (hand-over and resume) judge each entry whose memory now
differs from its submit copy: GPU-written pages, deferred entries, empty-at-submit entries,
never-written copies (zeros where memory has commands), copies that do not walk clean from the
carry there, and entries after an unknown carry take memory as before; every other entry keeps its
submit copy, whether the shape changed or only data words. A resumed entry then parses that copy
from its resume word (Step, resume_from_copy). Carry at a resume: the stream's own (as
EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX); at the hand-over 0 at the list's first entry, then entry by entry. Ocarina of
Time on Switch 2 only (DESYNC_FIX's title gate).

Switches (read once at boot): EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY: 1 judge and count, memory taken as before;
2 act; 3 act, but lists copied during a suspension take memory (fallback if 2 hangs at a load);
unset, 0 or anything else off. Idle (one line) with EDEN_NX2_RESNAPSHOT=0; stays off (one line)
with EDEN_NX2_JUNK_GUARD=1, EDEN_NX2_PARK_SPLIT_METHODS or EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_PARSE_CHECK. Works next to
DESYNC_FIX (counted apart); do not combine them in tests.
Test aid EDEN_TEST_FRAME_WAIT_MS=<ms> (nx2_gsv.h WaitForFrame): the present gives up after <ms>
(10-60000) instead of 4000 so a warm start can be made to run ahead; unset, 0 or not a number: 4000
and the old lines. Never in a play env. EDEN_UP_OOT_FRONT_WAIT's WaitForFrameFront keeps its own
4000 ms; with it the aid shortens only the fallback wait.
Log (HW_GPU warnings): boot "EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY=2 on: keeps a command entry's submit copy at a
refresh (hand-over and resume) when memory differs and the copy walks clean; ..."; at the first
refresh "... active: Ocarina of Time on Switch 2 (program ...)" or "... stays off: not Ocarina";
per acting refresh (first 256, then every 1024th) "EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY=2 action N: kept the
submit copy of K of D differing entries of a E-entry list at the hand-over|a resume (list copied
before|during the suspension), first at ...: W words differ, H header words differ; took memory for
M" (=1: "would keep (count only, took memory)"); every 10 s "EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY=2 10 s: R list
refreshes (...), D entries differed from their submit copy: kept the copy K (...), M took memory
(g GPU-written, d deferred, n never written, c copy does not walk clean, u carry unknown, s copied
during a suspension), f kept by EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX; resumed entries parsed from the copy P; since
boot kept T, X took memory"; the "Refresh check N:" summary gains "; EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY kept
the submit copy of K of them". Aid (Service): "EDEN_TEST_FRAME_WAIT_MS=250: the present gives up on
its frame's fence after 250 ms instead of 4000 (test aid: lets the game run ahead; never for
play)", every 10 s "EDEN_TEST_FRAME_WAIT_MS=250 10 s: G of W frame waits gave up (T since boot)",
and the give-up line reads "... not reached in 250 ms (now N; EDEN_TEST_FRAME_WAIT_MS)".

Not in TranslationSwitches (no shader change). Not a live switch.

Cost when off: one cached read per refresh (ResumeKeepCopyActing returns 0); the hand-over path,
the resume verdicts, Step's parse rule and the Refresh check line (empty suffix) unchanged. Aid
unset: the deadline is 4000 ms from a cached static, the old give-up text, one cached bool test per
frame wait. Behaviour byte for byte as before; the machine code is not.

Default flip (later, after the cold A/B and the normal-play check pass): video_core/dma_pusher.cpp,
anonymous namespace after RefreshCheckEventLogged: "constexpr int ResumeKeepCopyDefault = 0;" -> 2.
The aid never gets a default.

Risks: a list the CPU really patches after submit on pages no GPU work wrote would run its old
words (none seen: 0 of 7,675,038 copies differed with the full wait); about 3% of lists start with a
method open, the carry-0 guess then falls back to memory (today's behaviour) for the rest of that
list; a kept copy can wait exactly on a counter the game already passed (a wait that never ends:
"Channel N waits on semaphore ... (op 1, X, now Y)" with X below Y after an action line); mixed
frames stay possible through entries still read from memory.

Origin and credit: our own work (first-start crash of 12 Nov 2026). Draft
drafts-2026-11-11/ports-7/first-start/keep-submit-copy/draft.diff, placed unchanged (review:
ready to place). Merge: patch 0588 (EDEN_UP_FRAME_WAIT_PROGRESS) builds on this patch's
WaitForFrame deadline line.
